3) To calculate the total amount that the adults will eat: 20 dinosaurs * 10 lbs/dinosaur = \boxed{200 lbs}
4) To calculate the total amount that the children will eat: 5 dinosaurs * 5 lbs/dinosaur = \boxed{25 lbs}
5) Add the total amounts for the adults and children to get the total amount of potato salad needed: 200 lbs + 25 lbs = \boxed{225 lbs}

So Ted needs to bring \boxed{225 lbs} of potato salad to the picnic to make sure there is enough to feed everyone.
